ADDITIONS={
1:("Nina asks Leo about his day. He answers slowly. They do not know every word, but they can ask for help.",''),
2:("He leaves his book on the table. It is easy to see, and he can find it quickly after dinner.",''),
11:("They check the corrected bill together before paying. The mistake is now clear, and there is no need to argue about the whole meal. At home, they practise a short request: Could you check this item, please? A calm question can help when something seems wrong.","On my second shift, a different customer asked about opening hours. I checked the notice instead of guessing from memory. The shop closed earlier on that particular day. I learned that being helpful sometimes means taking a moment to find accurate information before giving a confident answer."),
12:("The new key works, and the room is quiet enough for his plans. Marcus puts the reception number beside the phone. If another problem occurs, he can explain it directly. He also keeps his booking confirmation, because it shows which services were included in the agreed price.","On the return journey, we arrive earlier and read the board together. This time the platform changes shortly before departure. We listen to the announcement and check the new number. Knowing the usual platform is useful, but current information is more important when arrangements have changed."),
13:("The experience changes how she checks future purchases. She tests the new lamp soon after bringing it home and keeps its packaging until she knows it works properly. She also reads the return conditions. A receipt is useful evidence, but different shops may offer different remedies.","The restaurant asks us to confirm the final number the day before the meal. We write that deadline beside the booking details. Everyone knows whom to contact if their plans change. This small arrangement helps us avoid giving the restaurant several different answers from different members of the group."),
14:("Afterwards, the team writes the agreed actions in a shared note. Someone who missed the meeting can see what changed and which deadline still applies. A suggestion made during discussion is marked separately from a confirmed decision. This prevents an unfinished idea from being treated as an instruction.","Before the next lesson, I check the weather and arrange a meeting place with my instructor. I do not invite friends to join yet, because I want to concentrate on the new route. My confidence is growing, but I still need practice before choosing a busy road alone."),
15:("The volunteer also notes who supplied the updated information. If someone later questions the time, the team knows whom to contact. The old message is kept but clearly marked as replaced. This is safer than leaving two different times visible with no explanation of which one is current.","Some phrases still feel difficult after several reviews. I keep them in the list, but I do not spend the whole evening on them. I choose one useful example and continue with listening or speaking. A balanced session helps me practise more than recognizing words on a page."),
16:("A borrower asks whether returning an item early means paying less. Staff explain the rule before accepting the booking. They also show where to report a problem with a tool. Reading these details matters because a low price does not explain every condition attached to a shared service.","After the first month, I review my attendance and the speaking tasks I have completed. I have missed only one class and can explain familiar situations more easily. I still find listening difficult. I decide to keep the course and add short listening practice instead of changing everything immediately."),
17:("Rosa keeps the photographs and repair messages together. If the same problem returns, she can describe what was repaired and when. She does not need to accuse anyone before the cause is known. A clear record makes a later request more specific and easier for the company to investigate.","The next morning, I tell reception that the quieter room solved the immediate problem. I also suggest mentioning the building work before guests arrive. Other guests may have different needs. Accurate information would allow them to choose a room or discuss alternatives before they are trying to sleep."),
18:("The team decides to review the arrangement after another month. People can suggest changes privately if they prefer. This makes it easier for someone to explain a practical difficulty without speaking in front of everyone. The habit remains voluntary, and participation is not included in ordinary work-performance ratings.","I save the studio number before the class so I can call even if the online message will not load. I also check which location my friend plans to use. We do not assume we have both seen the same update. A quick confirmation can prevent a wasted journey."),
19:("Before enrolling, he checks the full timetable against his work calendar. He asks which lessons contain practical tasks that are hard to replace with notes. This helps him judge the effect of a possible absence. A suitable level matters, but so does being able to attend regularly.","When the refund reaches my account, I compare the amount with the delivery charge on the receipt. It matches the agreement, so I close the complaint. I keep the final message with the order record. An apology was welcome, but checking the actual payment confirmed that the promised action happened."),
20:("They also write down who should be contacted for different problems. A delay involving the moving company needs one contact, while an issue with the new home may need another. Keeping these details together reduces confusion. It does not mean every unexpected event can be predicted in advance.","The coordinator invites applicants to visit the garden before accepting a plot. Seeing the space helps them judge whether they can manage the work. One applicant decides to volunteer on shared tasks instead. That is still a useful way to participate, even without taking responsibility for a separate plot.")
}
